    "gloss": "in, at (locative modifier: 於日中俯臥 -> 日中に於いて俯臥せしむ). The split is お + いて, not おい + て. KANJIDIC2 lists both boundaries for this one character — おい.て (= 於て) and お.ける (= 於ける) — and the second is the one to follow: 於いて and 於ける are the same stem お-, so a boundary that moves between them is describing two different characters. 於いて is also the ordinary modern spelling of the phrase this entry glosses. NOTE: this entry cannot reach either panel as things stand. `yuReading` in conjugationContext.ts answers for every token whose lemma is 於, and both KundokuView.ts and generator.ts consult it ahead of the override lookup, so 於 never arrives here — it renders as 於ヨリ (okurigana slot, no furigana) unless its governor is one of `LOCATIVE_GOVERNOR_LEMMAS`. The entry is the reading half of the change and is live in the token inspector; the panels reach it only once `yuReading` declines at these two deps. See the report"
