    "gloss": "about, roughly (approximative particle after a measure: 長三寸許 -> 長さ三寸ばかり). Here rather than in `SUPPLEMENTARY_KUN` because ばかり is a grammar word, and this table is the one that says so: an entry here is returned `spellOutInProse`, which writes ばかり in kana in the 書き下し文 and puts it in the 訓読文's okurigana slot instead of as furigana over the character — the treatment every other particle in this table gets, and the treatment 許 wants. A supplementary kun would have kept the kanji and given it furigana, which is right for a content word and wrong for this. Unconditioned, and the two things that could have made it conditional both turn out not to need it. (a) The verb 許す is untouched: VERB_LEXICON holds 許 as ゆる 四段サ行 and both panels consult it ahead of the resolver for a VERB/AUX token, which an entry with no beatsLexicon does not stand down. (b) The other NOUN sense is もと (母の許, 'at his mother's place'), which this entry does claim — a cost accepted rather than overlooked, since the parser gives both senses the same tag (NOUN) and no dep tells them apart. 酒蟲 has 許 twice and both are the approximative: 長三寸許 (sent_id 25), and the 許 the parser opened sent_id 21 with, which it tagged a place name (n,名詞,固定物,地名) after the source's comma cut 去首半尺許 in two"
